  <prompt>
    Implement FR-13 + FR-16: enrich the Compose redline contract with (1) a coarse
    `confidence_band` (`high` | `medium` | `low`) that is DERIVED SERVER-SIDE from
    grounding/verifiability evidence — is the change supported by a cited source / the retained
    original / the re-anchor score? — and (2) an explicit `paraId` + `start_offset` / `end_offset`
    on the redline anchor (these ride the E2 paraId substrate landed by task 012). Both are
    **additive, mirror-first** fields on `ComposeDraftPayload` (client mirror
    `types/compose-contracts.ts` &lt;-&gt; server record `ComposeDraftPayload` in
    `Services/Compose/ComposeDraftDisposition.cs`), snake_case, Tier-3-safe (enum/number, NOT user
    content). This is a DERIVATION change on the existing dispatch path — there is **NO new AI
    dispatch endpoint and NO AI catalog Action / row change** (engine frozen, NFR-04). The band is
    computed from grounding signals already present on the session output; if no grounding signal
    exists for an action, the band is `low` (or omitted) rather than guessed — never a false-precision
    numeric self-report. Do NOT auto-accept or pre-select on the band here (that is task 031's UI rule).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior full-stack engineer fluent in .NET 8 Minimal API record contracts + `System.Text.Json`
    `[JsonPropertyName]` snake_case serialization, and the TypeScript mirror discipline
    (`Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/types`). Comfortable reasoning about grounding/verifiability
    evidence as a server-side derivation and keeping `Services/Compose/` free of AI internals
    (ADR-013 facade).
  </role>

  <goal>
    An additive `confidence_band` field (`high` | `medium` | `low` enum) on `ComposeDraftPayload`
    — server record + client mirror — populated by a server-side derivation from existing grounding
    evidence (cited source presence / retained-original support / re-anchor score), plus additive
    `paraId` + `start_offset` / `end_offset` on `AnchoredAnnotationAnchor` (client) and its server
    counterpart, so a redline carries the exact paragraph identity + character offsets from the E2
    substrate. No new AI dispatch endpoint, no catalog row change, no AI-internal type injected into
    `Services/Compose/`. Matching tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/` cover the
    grounded=&gt;high / ungrounded=&gt;low derivation plus the additive-mirror round-trip; a through-the-wire
    seam slice test asserts the band + offsets survive the dispatch/serialize path.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      E3-rationale already ships: `ComposeDraftPayload` carries `target_text` / `new_text` /
      `match_mode` / `rationale` / `sources` / `edits[]` / `comments[]`, and the accept/reject
      popover already renders the rationale (design §2 redline-suggestion-payload row;
      `ComposeEditor.tsx:271-294`). The gap is a **confidence** signal and **explicit
      offsets/paraId** (design §6.1). Per the 2026 HCI research folded into design §6.2, a numeric
      confidence score is the weakest/riskiest signal (drives over-reliance + false precision), so
      E3 uses a **coarse qualitative band tied to verifiability**, derived server-side from grounding
      — NOT a raw model self-report. The offsets are only meaningful against a stable paragraph
      identity, so they RIDE E2 (task 012 landed paraId-primary anchoring + fuzzy fallback). This
      task adds the contract fields + the server derivation; task 031 designs the trust-semantics UI
      and task 032 handles formatted insertions.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDraftDisposition.cs — the `ComposeDraftPayload` record (line ~168; snake_case `[JsonPropertyName]`). Add `confidence_band` (enum) + anchor paraId/start_offset/end_offset additively; keep property-level boolean `required` BANNED (owner hygiene).</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/types/compose-contracts.ts — client mirror of `ComposeDraftPayload`; `AnchoredAnnotationAnchor` at lines 108-115 (`textPattern` + `paragraphHint`). Mirror the additive `confidence_band` + `paraId`/offsets; do NOT diverge the two shapes.</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs — Load/Save orchestration where the draft payload is materialized/dispatched; site of the server-side band derivation from grounding evidence (design §6.2). `LoadAsync` ~168 / draft materialization path.</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/AnnotationReanchorService.cs — the re-anchor scorer (Levenshtein) is one grounding/verifiability signal feeding the band derivation; the paraId substrate from task 012 is the other.</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/design.md §6 (E3 enriched redline contract — rationale-first, grounding-tied band, offsets-ride-E2, additive mirror-first, `required` BANNED), §2 (redline-payload + anchoring rows), §10 (reuse map — payload + re-anchor rows).</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/spec.md FR-13, FR-16, NFR-04, NFR-05, NFR-06.</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="012" status="pending">FR-11/FR-12 paraId-primary anchoring + fuzzy fallback + paraId as splice key. Provides the stable paragraph identity the offsets ride on; the re-anchor score it exposes is a grounding signal for the band derivation. Do not add offsets before the paraId substrate exists.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039 / NFR-04">Engine frozen: NO new AI dispatch endpoint and NO new/changed AI catalog rows (`sprk_analysisaction` / `sprk_analysisplaybook`). The band is SERVER-DERIVED from existing grounding evidence, not a new Action output field. If a band were ever model-supplied it would have to be declared in the JPS output schema + eval cases — this task deliberately keeps it derived to avoid that.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">`Services/Compose/` MUST NOT inject `IOpenAiClient`, executor, or routing types. The derivation consumes grounding signals already present on the session output / re-anchor service — no AI-internal reach. Tier-1 NetArchTest stays green. Use the `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` facade if any AI-produced grounding evidence is read.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / owner hygiene">Additive, mirror-first: the server record and the client mirror change together and stay identical in shape. Property-level boolean `required` is BANNED. snake_case wire vocabulary (`confidence_band`, `start_offset`, `end_offset`). NO version suffix anywhere.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015 / Tier-3">`confidence_band` + offsets are enum/number metadata — Tier-3-safe, NOT user document content. Do not smuggle user text into these fields.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / design §6.2">Derive the band from verifiability: grounded (cited source / retained-original support / strong re-anchor score) =&gt; `high`; weakly supported =&gt; `medium`; unsupported / no grounding signal =&gt; `low` (or omit). Never emit a false-precision numeric self-report. Do NOT auto-accept / pre-select on the band in this task (UI rule is FR-14 / task 031).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06 / ADR-038">A save/load/dispatch contract change carries a through-the-wire `WebApplicationFactory` seam slice test (`tests/integration/seam/**`) asserting the band + offsets survive serialize/dispatch. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration/ctor-null tests. Unit-green != done.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029 / CLAUDE.md §10">Report BFF publish size absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (incl. PDBs — state the convention); this is a contract/derivation change (no NuGet add) so expect ~0 MB delta. Verify no new HIGH CVE. State the Placement Justification (extension of `Services/Compose`, no new surface).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Additive snake_case record contracts + client mirror; server-side grounding-tied confidence derivation; AI-facade isolation</topic>
