    <output type="report">Publish-size absolute + delta; CVE scan; NetArchTest facade result; Placement Justification</output>
  </outputs>

  <justification>
    <existing>`ComposeDraftPayload` (server record + client mirror) already carries the redline contract (`rationale`/`sources`/`edits[]`); `AnchoredAnnotationAnchor` already carries `textPattern`/`paragraphHint`. This task adds FIELDS to those existing types — it does not introduce a new type, service, endpoint, or catalog row.</existing>
    <extension>Extend the existing record + mirror rather than create a parallel confidence contract: the band + offsets are properties of the redline the payload already models, and the derivation folds into the existing draft-materialization path in `ComposeService`. A new type would fork the mirror discipline and orphan the existing accept/reject render path.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the additive fields, FR-13 (grounding-tied confidence band renders `high`/`low`) and FR-16 (redline round-trips to the exact paragraph + offset) cannot be met — the accept/reject surface has no verifiability signal and redlines cannot anchor to an exact offset. Concrete failing contract: FR-13/FR-16 acceptance.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">A grounded suggestion (cited source / retained-original support / strong re-anchor score) renders `confidence_band: high`; an ungrounded one renders `low` — asserted by a server-side derivation unit test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No AI catalog row (`sprk_analysisaction` / `sprk_analysisplaybook`) and no AI dispatch endpoint is added or modified; the band is server-derived from existing grounding evidence (NFR-04).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`confidence_band` + `paraId` + `start_offset` / `end_offset` are additive, snake_case, present identically on the server `ComposeDraftPayload` record and the client `types/compose-contracts.ts` mirror; no property-level boolean `required` is introduced.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A redline round-trips to the exact paragraph (`paraId`) + character offset (`start_offset`/`end_offset`) — asserted through the dispatch/serialize path (FR-16).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`Services/Compose/` injects no AI-internal type (ADR-013 NetArchTest green); `confidence_band`/offsets carry enum/number metadata only (Tier-3-safe), never user document content.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A through-the-wire `WebApplicationFactory` seam slice test (`tests/integration/seam/**`) asserts the band + offsets survive the dispatch/serialize path (NFR-06); no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;` / DI-registration / ctor-null tests.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish size reported absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline, ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE; BFF + client shared-lib builds green with matching tests passing.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
